module rln_gifter_module {
  version "0.6.0"
  depends []

  method request(args_json: tstr) -> tstr description "Client: request a gifted membership from an allocator. Args\n`{config?, identityCommitment, rate?, authType?, authPayload?,\n authProvider?, authArgs?, discover?, gifterPeerId?, gifterMultiaddr?}`.\nconfig names the registry (ConfigState account). Allocators\nadvertising the (registry, authType) pair through libp2p service\ndiscovery are tried first (discover, default true; needs config and a\nnode with discovery mounted) while none has read the request; the\nconfigured gifterPeerId+gifterMultiaddr pair, if any, comes after\nthem. authType names the auth vector in the wire's OPEN\nauthentication_type vocabulary — any type the target gifter's\nauthVerifiers accept; this module knows no vector by name. The payload\ncomes from authPayload (raw hex, verbatim) or an authProvider module\nimplementing the rln_auth_vector producer contract (authArgs forwarded\nverbatim); no authType at all is an unauthenticated request for an\nopen gifter\n→ `{leaf_index, id_commitment, auth_success, identity_adopted,\n gifterPeerId, discovered, tx_hash?, config_account?}`. With nothing\ngranted and no pair configured, the reply is `{error: \"no allocator\ngranted and none is configured: <why>\"}`, <why> being\n`discovery unavailable: <msg>` (this node cannot discover),\n`discovery not joined: no connected peer after 20s` or\n`no allocator advertises <registry>/<authType>` (both may clear on a\nlater request)."
  method discover(args_json: tstr) -> tstr description "Client: the allocators currently advertising a (registry, authType)\npair through libp2p service discovery. Args `{config, authType?}`.\nThe client registers interest, waits up to 20 s for an outbound peer,\nthen looks up at 0, 2, 4 and 8 s\n→ `{serviceId, candidates:[{peerId, addrs}], joined, peers}` (joined:\nan outbound peer was connected; peers: how many; candidates empty when\nnone is placed yet); `{error: \"discovery unavailable: <msg>\"}` when\nthis node has no discovery mounted."
  method serve(args_json: tstr) -> tstr description "Gifter node: mount the gifter protocol and serve inbound requests. Args\n`{config, wallet, registries?, authVerifiers?, consumedNullifiersPath?,\n maxRateLimit?, advertise?, advertiseAddrs?}` → `{mounted:true,\n registries, advertised, advertisedToPeers?, serviceId?, serviceData?,\n advertiseError?}`. advertiseAddrs (multiaddrs) puts exactly those\naddresses in the advertised record (a signed record this module\nrefreshes every 600 s); without it libp2p publishes the listen\naddresses. The first advertisement waits up to 20 s for an outbound\npeer; the worker re-advertises when peers appear after an\nadvertisement placed with none.\nauthVerifiers maps each accepted authentication_type to its verifier\nmodule (`{\"<type>\": {module, config?}}` — an rln_auth_vector\nVERIFY_METHOD implementor; config rides along opaquely on every\ncall). ALL vectors are such plugins — this module ships none. No\nauthVerifiers = an open gifter. advertise (default true) publishes\nthe served (registry, type) pairs under the protocol id through\nlibp2p service discovery; a node without discovery mounted serves\nunadvertised (advertiseError says so) unless advertise is an explicit\ntrue, which makes that an error."
  method libp2p_call(args_json: tstr) -> tstr description "Relay an arbitrary libp2p_module call so the UI can read its return value\n(a C++ LogosResult marshals to null through the QML bridge; a module-to-\nmodule SDK call returns the real value). `{method, args}` → the reply JSON.\nUsed by the app to bring up the libp2p node (rlnEnable/start) before request."
}
